# Code owners: the maintainer owns every path .github/risk-assessment.yml rates
# high (docs/risk-tiers.md): CI and gates, gate tooling, Flatpak manifests, the
# build, the metainfo and settings schema, the data schemas, and agent
# instructions. A pull request that touches one requests his review. Medium-
# and low-risk paths have no owner.
#
# Keep this file and the high-risk rules in step: tests/tooling/test_codeowners.py
# fails if a tracked file is high risk but unowned, or owned but not high risk.
# Patterns use .gitignore syntax: a leading `/` anchors to the repository root,
# and `*` does not cross `/` (the risk rules' `*` does, so a rule such as
# `data/*.metainfo.xml.in` is written out per directory here).

# CI gates, review rubric, rulesets, the risk rules, and this file itself.
/.github/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Gate tooling: CI scripts, the submission validator, the popularity pipeline.
/scripts/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Flatpak manifests: sandbox permissions (finish-args), runtime, sources.
/build-aux/                         @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# The build, its options and the release version.
/meson.build                        @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/meson_options.txt                  @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Release notes and branding, and stored settings.
/data/*.metainfo.xml.in             @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/data/*.gschema.xml.in              @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# The data contract with every installed copy of the app.
/data/v1/schema/                    @Tim-van-Oudheusden

# Agent instructions and governance.
/AGENTS.md                          @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/CLAUDE.md                          @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/.claude/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/.cursor/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden
/prompts/                           @Tim-van-Oudheusden
